## Status

Accepted. `cloud-itonami-isic-2821` scaffolded fresh, tested green, and
promoted `:spec` -> `:implemented` in `kotoba-lang/industry`.

## Context

ISIC 2821 (\"Manufacture of agricultural and forestry machinery\") had
only a legacy placeholder entry in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry
(`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2821`, `:maturity :spec`). Per this fleet's
smaller-batch rollout discipline following a prior 18-agent haiku
batch's 61% defect rate, this build follows the stricter verified
protocol (capable model, mandatory fresh-clone re-verification) that
96+ consecutive prior agents in this fleet have completed successfully.

Before any work began, the registry's live `:name` for `{:id \"2821\"
...}` was verified via the GitHub git blob API (not the CDN-cached
`raw.githubusercontent.com`) against a fresh clone: it reads exactly
\"Manufacture of agricultural and forestry machinery\", confirming the
assigned premise. `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821`
returned 404 before scaffolding started, confirming no prior attempt
exists to build on or revert to.

The closest domain analog and mirrored reference is
`cloud-itonami-isic-2826` (Manufacture of machinery for textile,
apparel and leather production, 77 tests / 210 assertions): both are
back-office plant-operations-coordination actors for a fixed
manufacturing plant with electromechanically-assembled, test-bench-
verified finished-goods output and a real physical/worker safety
dimension.

## Decision

Scaffolded `cloud-itonami-isic-2821` as a fresh standalone repo
(`AgMachAdvisor ⊣ Agricultural and Forestry Machinery Plant Operations
Governor`, langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger),
mirroring `cloud-itonami-isic-2826`'s verified module shape
module-for-module (`agmachmfg.*` in place of `texmachmfg.*`):

- **Equipment/product vocabulary adapted to the vertical**:
  `:tractor-assembly-line`/`:harvester-test-bench` equipment kinds in
  place of loom-assembly/sewing-machine-test-bench;
  `:tractor`/`:combine-harvester`/`:tillage-implement`/`:baler`/
  `:forestry-harvester` product-type closed set in place of weaving-
  loom/sewing-machine/leather-cutting-machine/knitting-machine/fabric-
  cutting-machine; `:pto-no-load-speed-rpm` (plausibility-checked
  0-1200 rpm, informed by the ISO 500 series' nominal PTO speeds of
  540/1000 rpm with test-bench headroom, and the ISO 4254 series'
  general mechanical/hydraulic-safety framework) in place of
  `:no-load-run-speed-rpm`.
- **Four ops, all `:effect :propose` only**: `:log-production-batch`
  (batch product-type/PTO-no-load-speed/quantity/defect-rate data
  logging), `:schedule-maintenance` (assembly/test-bench-equipment
  maintenance scheduling proposal), `:flag-safety-concern` (mechanical-
  safety/hydraulic-hazard/PTO-guard-compliance concern -- ALWAYS
  escalates regardless of confidence), `:coordinate-shipment`
  (outbound product shipment coordination proposal).
- **HARD invariants (twelve concrete governor checks, no override)**:
  plant/batch record (equipment for maintenance, batch for shipment)
  must be independently verified/registered before any action;
  request `:effect` must be `:propose` only; the proposal's own
  `:effect` must be within the closed propose-shaped allowlist (no
  direct assembly/test-bench-equipment control); directly actuating
  assembly/test-bench equipment (`:actuate-equipment? true`) is a
  PERMANENT, unconditional block; self-issuing a machinery safety
  certification mark (`:issue-certification? true`, any op -- e.g. CE
  marking under the EU Machinery Directive, or ROPS certification
  under the OECD Standard Codes for the Official Testing of
  Agricultural and Forestry Tractors) is a PERMANENT, unconditional
  block; a shipment may not push a batch's own recorded shipped
  quantity past its own logged production quantity (independently
  recomputed, never self-reported); no double-scheduling the same
  maintenance record; no fabricated `:product-type`; no physically
  implausible `:pto-no-load-speed-rpm` or `:defect-rate-percent`; the
  op allowlist is closed to the four ops above.
- **Phase 0->3 rollout**: `:schedule-maintenance`/`:flag-safety-
  concern`/`:coordinate-shipment` are NEVER in any phase's `:auto` set
  (permanent, matching the governor's own posture); only
  `:log-production-batch` (no physical/financial risk) may auto-commit
  at phase 3 when governor-clean.
- **No pre-existing capability library to wrap** (verified: no
  `kotoba-lang/agmachmfg`-style repo exists) -- self-contained pure-
  function domain logic in `agmachmfg.registry`, independently
  re-verified by `agmachmfg.governor`, the same \"ground truth, not
  self-report\" discipline established across prior actors.
- The blueprint's own `:itonami.blueprint/governor` keyword,
  `:agricultural-forestry-machinery-plant-operations-governor`, is
  grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide before this repo was created.

Full module set (`registry.cljc`/`governor.cljc`/`advisor.cljc`/
`phase.cljc`/`store.cljc`/`operation.cljc`/`sim.cljc` + `deps.edn` +
`blueprint.edn` + governance/license docs) shipped in one fresh
scaffold. All source is `.cljc` (portable ClojureScript/JVM/nbb) with
no JVM-only interop, per this workspace's cljs-first runtime
priority. The actor graph is invoked exclusively via
`langgraph.graph/run*` (not `.invoke`, not cljs-portable).

## Verification

- `clojure -M:test` from the initial scaffold: `Ran 77 tests
  containing 210 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.`
- `clojure -M:lint` (clj-kondo): `linting took 995ms, errors: 0,
  warnings: 0`.
- `clojure -M:dev:run` demo narrative exercises proposal submission,
  escalation and every HARD-hold scenario directly (not-propose-
  effect, unknown-op, equipment-not-verified, batch-not-verified,
  shipment-quantity-exceeded, equipment-actuate-blocked,
  certification-authority-blocked, already-scheduled, invalid-product-
  type, invalid-pto-no-load-speed, invalid-defect-rate) -- confirmed
  by inspecting the printed audit ledger (4 commits, 12 holds, no
  exceptions).
- Pushed to `https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821`
  main at commit `722faa056bbf5a3237d20e2f9bb893872c34e461`.
- **Independently re-verified from a brand-new fresh clone** (separate
  temp directory, `kotoba-lang/langgraph` + `kotoba-lang/langchain`
  re-cloned as siblings): `clojure -M:test` again reports `Ran 77
  tests containing 210 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` at the same
  commit.
- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry: `\"2821\"` entry's `:maturity` flipped
  `:spec` -> `:implemented`, `:repo`/`:business-id` updated from the
  legacy `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2821` placeholder to
  `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821` via an exact-text in-place
  edit of only that entry's block (GitHub Contents API, blob-SHA
  match, no other entry touched). `industry_test.clj`'s
  `:implemented` count assertion recomputed from the live file via
  `kotoba.industry/maturity-summary` and bumped; full registry suite
  re-run green before pushing. See PR/merge details recorded in this
  ADR's companion EDN and the registry repo's own commit history.

## Consequences

(+) ISIC 2821 now has a real, tested, governed plant-operations-
coordination actor instead of a legacy placeholder spec entry.

(+) Vertical-specific hazard vocabulary (PTO entanglement, hydraulic
hazard, ROPS certification) is explicit in the governor's domain
model rather than reused verbatim from a dissimilar vertical.

(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer -- no integration with real
plant-management databases, freight dispatch or certification-body
APIs. Equipment actuation and certification issuance remain human-/
